  "body_markdown": "(310)-481-0111\n\nDental Implants\n\nDental Implant Surgery\n\nAll-on-4® Dental Implants\n\nHybrid Fixed Detachable Denture\n\nZirconia Fixed Bridge\n\nImplant Supported Dentures\n\nRobotic Surgery\n\nCost & Compare\n\nWhat To Expect\n\nFAQ\n\nAesthetic Dentistry\n\nCosmetic Dentistry\n\nPorcelain Veneers & Lumineers\n\nInvisalign\n\nTeeth Whitening\n\nSmile Makeover\n\nServices\n\nIV Sedation\n\nBone Grafting\n\nRidge Augmentation\n\nSinus Augmentation\n\nTooth Extractions\n\nGeneral Dentistry\n\nPeriodontics\n\nConditions We Treat\n\nMissing Teeth\n\nBone Loss\n\nFailing Dental Implants\n\nLoose Dentures\n\nPatient Center\n\nInsurance & Financing\n\nOur Facility\n\nPatient Stories\n\nBefore & After Photos\n\nWho We Are\n\nCommitment To Excellence\n\nMeet Dr. Tony Barriere\n\nMeet The Team\n\nVideo Library\n\nBlog\n\nContact Us\n\nPatient Portal\n\nNew Patients\n\nCurrent Patients\n\n\n## Should I Get Dental Implants After A Bone Grafting Procedure?\n\n\nJanuary 19, 2023\n\n\n#### Share This Post\n\n\nShare on facebook\n\nShare on linkedin\n\nShare on twitter\n\nShare on email\n\nDental implants are a popular treatment option for those who are missing teeth or are experiencing damaged or broken teeth that need repair. Dental implants in Los Angeles, CA, are most successful when they are placed on a sturdy and solid jawbone. If a trained doctor determines that a person’s jawbone is not sturdy enough to support dental implants, then that person may need to receive a bone grafting procedure first.\n\nAfter getting a bone grafting procedure, patients can have a successful dental implant procedure that can last for years to come. There are various other reasons why patients should get dental implants after a bone grafting procedure.\n\n\n## What Happens During A Bone Grafting Procedure\n\n\nWhile people with missing teeth may want to get them replaced right away with dental implants, that may not be possible unless they get a bone grafting treatment first. A bone grafting procedure is typically done when there is not enough bone in the jaw to support the implant. Bone grafting can help improve the long-term success of dental implants by increasing the amount of available bone.\n\nDuring a bone grafting procedure, the bone graft material is placed in the area of the jaw where bone has deteriorated. After the bone graft has been sutured into place and the patient has healed from the procedure, the patient can be a candidate for dental implants in Los Angeles, CA.\n\n\n## Why Should I Get Dental Implant’s After A Bone Grafting Procedure?\n\n\nAfter getting a bone grafting procedure, patients should get treated with dental implants in Los Angeles, CA, so that the jawbone can remain healthy and strong. Dental implants can help keep the jawbone healthy and strong because of the dental implant post. The dental implant post is made to act like a natural tooth root, stimulating the jawbone into health and strength. With a healthy and strong jawbone, a patient’s dental implants can be successfully stabilized in the patient’s mouth.\n\nAfter the dental implant is stabilized in the patient’s healthy new jawbone, the abutment can be placed on top. An abutment is what connects the dental implant post to the crown or prosthesis. Finally, the prosthesis or dental crowns is placed on top of the dental implant, giving patients a stable, natural looking, and functional new smile. With proper care and maintenance, dental implants can last for years to come.\n\n\n## Get Your Dental Implants With Us Now!\n\n\nWith a bone grafting treatment, you can achieve your best smile yet with dental implants. Get in contact with our doctors, Dr. Tony Barriere, at our office by Los Angeles, CA to schedule your consultation with us today. Your new smile could be just a few appointments away.\n\nPrevPreviousDental Implant Posts Can Improve Your Oral Health\n\nNextIs It Possible For Me To Get Customized Dental Implant Treatments?Next\n\n\n#### More To Explore\n\n\n\n### Are There Factors That Determine Which Type Of Dental Implant Procedure I Can Get Treated With?\n\n\nDental implants in Los Angeles, FL, are a safe and effective way to replace missing or damaged teeth. They are\n\nRead More »\n\nAugust 20, 2023\n\n\n### Does Anything Happen To My Jawbone If I Don’t Immediately Replace My Missing Teeth With Dental Implants?\n\n\nDental implants in Los Angeles, FL, are a gold standard tooth replacement option that are surgically placed in a patient’s\n\nAugust 14, 2023\n\n\n## You Are Welcome Here.\n\n\nSchedule your consultation today.\n\nCall Now\n\nFacebook Instagram Youtube Yelp Google\n\n\n#### Contact Us\n\n\nAddress:\n\n12301 Wilshire Blvd Suite 205,\n\nLos Angeles, CA 90025\n\n(310) 481-0111\n\n\n#### Hours\n\n\nMonday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nTuesday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nWednesday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nThursday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nFriday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nSaturday: Closed\n\nSunday: Closed\n\n\n#### Services\n\n\n\n#### About Us\n\n\nPrivacy Policy\n\nDental Website by Progressive Dental Marketing",
